          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
            is its left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            of its domain to a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat F : PSh(C) \to D
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            there should be a corresponding version of this construction.
          %p
            In particular with categories replaced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-catgeories
            there should be a version with the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            replaced by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma+for+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} Yoneda lemma for (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            This in turn should have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            in terms of the global
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %h2#statement Statement
          .standout
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              \: this here is something I thought about. Check. Even to the extent that this is right, it is clearly not yet a full answer, but at best a step in the right direction.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi proj
                  %mo =
                  %mi SPSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, SSet]_{proj} = SPSh(C)_{proj}
            for the projective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}
            be any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
          .un_proposition
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              takes values in cofibrant objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}
              then the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat F
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              part of an
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat F : SPSh(C)_{proj}
                    \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{D}
                    \:
                    R
                    \\,.
          %p
            Accordingly, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            does not take values in cofibrant objects but where a cofibrant replacement functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q : \mathbf{D} \to \mathbf{D}
            is given, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mi F
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{Q F}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q F
            is an
            = succeed "-extension" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %h3#proof Proof
          %p We prove this in two steps.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : SPSh(C)_{proj} \to \mathbf{D}
              preserves cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Recall that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : SPSh(C)_{proj} \to \mathbf{D}
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
              formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat F : X \mapsto \int^{U \in C} F(U) \cdot X(U)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where in the integrand we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensoring
              of the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(U) \in \mathbf{D}
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(U)
            %p
              The lemma now rests on the fact that this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int (-)\cdot (-)
                    \:
                    [C,\mathbf{D}]_{inj}
                    \\cdot
                    [C^{op}, SSet]_{proj}
                    \\to
                    \\mathbf{D}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
              using the injective and projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+functors"} global model structure on functors
              as indicated. This is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT prop. A.2.9.26 rmk. A.2.9.27
              and recalled at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
            %p
              Since by assumption
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(U)
              is cofibrant for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat F
              itself is cofibrant regarded as an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi D
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,\mathbf{D}]_{inj}
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi U
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat F = \int^U F(U) \cdot (-)(U) : SPSh(C)_{proj} \to \mathbf{D}
            %p preserves cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations.
          .un_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat F
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R : \mathbf{D} \to \mathrm{SPSh}(C)
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R(A)
                    \=
                    \\mathbf{D}(F(-), A)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p This is a standard argument.
            %p
              We demonstrate the Hom-isomorphism that characterizes the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            %p
              Start with the above
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
              description of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{D}({\hat F}(X), A)
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbf{D}(
                    \\int^{U \in S}
                    F(U) \cdot X(U)
                    ,
                    A
                    )
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then use the continuity of the enriched Hom-functor to pass it through the coend and obtain the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \simeq
                    \\int_{U \in S}
                    \\mathbf{D}({\hat F}(U) \cdot X(U), A)
                    \\,.
            %p The defining property of the tensoring operation implies that this is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\simeq
                    \\int_{U \in S}
                    SSet( X(U), \mathbf{D}(F(U),A))
                    \\,.
            %p
              But this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} end-formula
              for the
              = succeed "-object" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\simeq
                    [C^{op},SSet](X, \mathbf{D}(\Pi(-), A))
                    \\,.
            %p By definition this is the desired right hand of the hom isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \=  [C^{op}, SSet](X, R(A))
                    \\,.
          %p These two lemmas together constitute the proof of the proposition.
